## 2. Conflict resolution

In [WizardArtIntegrationTests.cs](/workspace/Assets/NoSafeCircle/DoorPrototype/Tests/Editor/WizardArtIntegrationTests.cs:130), I retained current main’s specific assertions for:

- Player and DoorSprite sorting layer/order.
- Both renderers using pivot sorting.
- The Player visual’s CharacterController skin-width ground offset.

The prep branch’s broader loop over every scene SpriteRenderer was omitted because unrelated world renderers need not all share the Player’s sorting settings. Its non-conflicting eight-direction builder checks were retained and expanded.

The classifier audit found no algorithm defect after the merge: it already has eight sectors, deterministic boundary ties, hysteresis, and idle-facing retention. The missing full eight-direction/runtime coverage was corrected in tests.

